  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>Licorice gouramis are ideal inhabitants of nano tanks. They should be kept in one-species tanks. They can reach an age of 5 or more years. The fish attain a length of about 3 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>Parosphromenus gunawani comes from the island of Sumatra, from the province of Jambi. It is a Parosphromenus species of the bintan type and was scientifically described only in 2012; previously it was known to specialized labyrinthfish enthusiasts as Parosphromenus sp. Danau Rasau.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>Licorice gouramis settle even in extreme natural habitats. The water there is very poor in nutrients, very soft and acidic.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>They can be fed exclusively with live brine shrimp nauplii (Artemia).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>In all licorice gouramis the sexes can be distinguished even in fright coloration. Both males and females look like Betta females in that mood, but the caudal fin of the females is completely hyaline, whereas in the caudal fin of the males an iridescent shine can always be observed that reflects the courtship coloration.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>They produce a low number of eggs per spawning, usually fewer than 20.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/parosphromenus-gunawani-2/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Parosphromenus means \"stands beside Osphromenus\"; Osphromenus is another genus of anabantid. bintan: after the island of Bintan, the type locality. gunawani: the species is named in honour of Gunawan 'Thomas' Kasim, who, together with Horst Linke and others, collected the type specimens of this taxon.</p>"
    }
  ],
